      "description": "Lesson segments as section-hue tabs on the fore edge; the current tab extends to the edge.",
      "html": "<ol class=\"ds-tabrail\"><li class=\"ds-tab ds-tab-done\" style=\"--hue:#e0672a;--on:#1b1a17\"><span>What is a PDA?</span><b>2:41</b></li><li class=\"ds-tab ds-tab-now\" style=\"--hue:#0e7d79;--on:#fff\"><span>Finding the bump</span><b>0:30</b></li><li class=\"ds-tab ds-tab-todo\" style=\"--hue:#3d7a30;--on:#fff\"><span>Signing</span><b>~3m</b></li></ol>",
      "css": ".ds-tabrail{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;width:54px;height:360px;}.ds-tab{flex:1;margin-left:8px;padding:10px 0;background:var(--hue);color:var(--on);border-radius:0 6px 6px 0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px;}.ds-tab span{writing-mode:vertical-rl;transform:rotate(180deg);font-family:'Archivo Variable','Archivo',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:750;font-stretch:78%;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;}.ds-tab b{font-family:'JetBrains Mono',ui-monospace,monospace;font-weight:400;font-size:10px;}.ds-tab-done{filter:saturate(0.55);}.ds-tab-todo{margin-left:14px;}.ds-tab-now{margin-left:0;box-shadow:-3px 0 0 #1b1a17 inset;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Punch",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "punch",
      "description": "A person as a punched hole on the binding edge, ringed in their colour; ink mark when ready.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-punch\" style=\"--who:#f2a93b\"><span class=\"ds-hole\">A</span><span class=\"ds-mark\"><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"/></svg></span></span>",
      "css": ".ds-punch{position:relative;display:inline-grid;place-items:center;}.ds-hole{width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:50%;display:grid;place-items:center;background:#ddd4bf;color:#1b1a17;box-shadow:inset 0 2px 3px rgba(40,30,10,0.35),0 0 0 3px var(--who);font-family:'Archivo Variable','Archivo',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;font-stretch:80%;}.ds-mark{position:absolute;right:-4px;bottom:-4px;width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:50%;display:grid;place-items:center;background:#1b1a17;color:#f2ede0;border:2px solid #f2ede0;}.ds-mark svg{width:10px;height:10px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Errata Slip",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "errata-slip",
      "description": "The one place vermilion fills a surface: an error, with what to do next.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-errata\" role=\"alert\"><svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.25\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><path d=\"M12 8v4M12 16h.01\"/></svg><span>The question did not send. Press Ask again.</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-errata{display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:flex-start;padding:9px 12px;background:#fbe3dc;border:1px solid #d93a1c;border-radius:2px;color:#6e1a09;font-family:'Archivo Variable','Archivo',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:0.8125rem;}.ds-errata svg{flex:none;margin-top:2px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Question Card",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "question-card",
      "description": "A flat entry ruled on the rail leaf; the inline answer reads in the serif.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-qcard\"><div class=\"ds-qhead\"><span class=\"ds-stamp ds-stamp-ok\">Answered</span></div><h4 class=\"ds-qtitle\">Is the program id part of the hash?</h4><p class=\"ds-qby\">You asked</p><p class=\"ds-qans\">Yes. The program id is hashed together with the seeds and the bump.</p></article>",
      "css": ".ds-qcard{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:7px;padding:11px 12px 12px;background:#fbf8f1;border:1px solid #cdc4ae;border-radius:3px;max-width:330px;font-family:'Archivo Variable','Archivo',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#1b1a17;}.ds-qhead{min-height:28px;display:flex;align-items:center;}.ds-stamp{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:20px;padding:1px 7px;border:1.5px solid currentColor;border-radius:2px;font-size:10.5px;font-weight:750;font-stretch:80%;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;}.ds-stamp-ok{color:#3f7f33;}.ds-qtitle{margin:0;font-size:0.9375rem;font-weight:680;font-stretch:86%;line-height:1.28;}.ds-qby{margin:0;font-size:0.72rem;color:#6b6557;font-weight:600;font-stretch:85%;letter-spacing:0.04em;}.ds-qans{margin:0;font-family:'Source Serif 4 Variable','Source Serif 4',Georgia,serif;font-size:0.98rem;line-height:1.5;padding-top:8px;border-top:1px solid #cdc4ae;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Check Option",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "check-option",
      "description": "Answer options across the check leaf; chosen takes ink and a yellow tint, keys in mono.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-opts\"><button class=\"ds-opt\" aria-pressed=\"true\"><span class=\"ds-key\">A</span>The program</button><button class=\"ds-opt\"><span class=\"ds-key\">B</span>The wallet</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-opts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(190px,1fr));gap:6px;}.ds-opt{display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;min-height:44px;padding:10px 12px;text-align:left;cursor:pointer;background:#fbf8f1;border:1.5px solid #a99f88;border-radius:3px;color:#1b1a17;font-family:'Archivo Variable','Archivo',system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:0.9375rem;transition:background 90ms steps(2),border-color 90ms steps(2);}.ds-opt:hover{border-color:#1b1a17;}.ds-opt[aria-pressed='true']{border-color:#1b1a17;background:#f8e8b6;}.ds-opt:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #1b1a17;outline-offset:2px;}.ds-key{font-family:'JetBrains Mono',ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#6b6557;padding-top:3px;}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Acetate Manual",
    "overview": "The live class is a boxed-software reference manual lying open at a tabbed section. The lesson is the manual: each segment is a coloured divider tab on the fore edge, the shared whiteboard is the printed leaf in the middle of the page, people are punched holes along the binding, and a private thread is a sheet of milk acetate hinged over the leaf so the class stays visible underneath. Everything is cream stock and black print ink; colour is spent only where it carries meaning (a section, an action, an error).\n\nDensity is that of a reference manual, not a dashboard: condensed Archivo running heads and labels, Source Serif 4 for anything meant to be read as prose (captions, tutor answers, notes), and JetBrains Mono only for numbers, codes and times. Nothing eases or fades. Every state change is a two-frame mechanical step of 90 ms, and board figures plot on in discrete pen-plotter steps. The world refuses the video-call grid with a chat sidebar: no faces tiled, no bubble chat, no glassy dark panels.\n\nThe world is light only. `color-scheme` is set to `light` on `:root`; there is no dark theme.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cream section board (paper), white printed leaf, milk acetate as the three material layers.",
      "Chrome yellow is the one action ink; vermilion is the one error ink.",
      "Six section hues on divider tabs, cycled per lesson segment.",
      "Condensed uppercase Archivo for heads, labels, stamps and buttons; serif for reading; mono for figures.",
      "Two-frame stepped motion (90 ms, `steps(2)`), hinged at the punched edge; never eased.",
      "Lucide line icons only; no emoji."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Yellow Rule",
        "body": "Chrome yellow fills only the primary pressable action, and only while it can be pressed: a disabled primary drops to a transparent outline (the Send button only turns yellow once there is something to send). Never a section hue, never decoration, never a status.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Errata Rule",
        "body": "Vermilion appears only when something failed or would destroy something. It is never a section hue and never emphasis.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Section Ink Rule",
        "body": "A segment's hue belongs to that segment's tab and the few marks that say \"this part of the lesson\"; it is never used for actions or errors.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono-for-Figures Rule",
        "body": "JetBrains Mono sets only numbers, codes, times and keys (seat counts, 0:30, invite codes, option letters, segment numbers, code on the board). Never words, never headings.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Serif-Is-Speech Rule",
        "body": "If it is prose to be read (what the tutor says, what the class wrote down), it is Source Serif 4. Interface words stay in Archivo.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lies-On-Top Rule",
        "body": "A shadow means one sheet is laid over another. Question cards are ruled entries on the rail's leaf and stay flat; only the one that needs you (attention) takes the leaf shadow and an ink border.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Focus Economy Rule",
        "body": "While a check or thread is in play, what is not in play falls back to the page: desaturate to 0.3 to 0.35 and drop opacity to 0.5 to 0.6, in a two-frame step.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do give each surface at most one chrome yellow primary action, and let it lose its yellow while disabled.",
      "Do reserve vermilion for the errata slip, invalid fields, wrong answers and the destructive confirm.",
      "Do colour lesson segments only with the six section hues, in order (orange, teal, grass, ultramarine, violet, sienna), with ink on orange and white on the rest.",
      "Do set numbers, codes, times and keys in JetBrains Mono, and only those.",
      "Do set spoken and written prose (captions, tutor answers, notes, prompts) in Source Serif 4.",
      "Do animate in two-frame steps (`var(--step) steps(2)`, 90 ms) and hinge new leaves from the punched edge.",
      "Do say status in words on a stamp first; colour only reinforces.",
      "Do use lucide line icons (12 to 16px, stroke 2 to 3), with a short word beside them wherever there is room (host controls keep their words on phones).",
      "Do show people as punched holes ringed in their colour, never as avatars or video tiles.",
      "Do make the acetate opaque on phones while keeping its edge and shadow."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use yellow for a section, a status, a warning or decoration.",
      "Don't use vermilion for emphasis or as a section hue.",
      "Don't ease or fade transitions (no `ease`, `ease-in-out` or smooth cross-fades); step them.",
      "Don't use emoji anywhere in the interface; reactions and marks are lucide icons and words.",
      "Don't use mono for words, labels or headings.",
      "Don't round corners past 3px on leaves, buttons and inputs; only punches and swatches are circles.",
      "Don't raise every card; only a sheet laid over another, or the one entry that needs you, gets a shadow.",
      "Don't build a video-call grid or a bubble chat sidebar; the class is the manual.",
      "Don't add a dark theme by inverting tokens; the world is printed stock and is light only."
    ]
  }
}